Using dynamic import in a synchronous context wrapped in a Promise constructor is an anti-pattern. The dynamic import already returns a Promise, so the Promise constructor is unnecessary. Consider using async/await or returning the import directly.
```suggestion
async function checkSqliteBindings() {
  try {
    // Try to import and use better-sqlite3
    const Database = await import('better-sqlite3');
    try {
      const db = new Database.default(':memory:');
      db.close();
      return true;
    } catch (error) {
      console.log('SQLite bindings test failed:', error.message);
      return false;
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.log('SQLite module import failed:', error.message);
    return false;
  }
```

